<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Robert Fitzhamon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1107</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Robert Fitzhamon was a Norman baron who conquered the Welsh kingdom of Morgannwg around 1093, overthrowing its king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iestyn-ap-gwrgant">Iestyn ap Gwrgant</a>. He built a castle at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cardiff">Cardiff</a> inside the old Roman fort and granted the fertile <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vale-of-glamorgan">Vale of Glamorgan</a> to his knights, founding the Lordship of Glamorgan.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/robert-fitzhamon.jpg" alt="Robert Fitzhamon" width="320" height="445" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:RobertFitzHamon_BodleianMS_TopGloucD2.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
